https://help.eclipse.org/latest/index.jsp?topic=%2Forg.eclipse.jdt.doc.isv%2Freference%2Fapi%2Forg%2Feclipse%2Fjdt%2Fcore%2Fformatter%2FDefaultCodeFormatterConstants.html
https://github.com/google/styleguide/blob/gh-pages/eclipse-java-google-style.xml

Alignment value mapping:
value = wrap + indent + force

force:
0 = false
1 = true

indent:
0 = INDENT_DEFAULT
2 = INDENT_ON_COLUMN
4 = INDENT_BY_ONE

wrap:
0 = WRAP_NO_SPLIT
16 = WRAP_COMPACT
32 = WRAP_COMPACT_FIRST_BREAK
48 = WRAP_ONE_PER_LINE
64 = WRAP_NEXT_SHIFTED
80 = WRAP_NEXT_PER_LINE

Common values:
0  = false, WRAP_NO_SPLIT, INDENT_DEFAULT
16 = false, WRAP_COMPACT, INDENT_DEFAULT
32 = false, WRAP_COMPACT_FIRST_BREAK, INDENT_DEFAULT
48 = false, WRAP_ONE_PER_LINE, INDENT_DEFAULT
64 = false, WRAP_NEXT_SHIFTED, INDENT_DEFAULT
80 = false, WRAP_NEXT_PER_LINE, INDENT_DEFAULT

Add 1 for forceSplit=true, 2 for INDENT_ON_COLUMN, and 4 for INDENT_BY_ONE.
Examples:
49 = true, WRAP_ONE_PER_LINE, INDENT_DEFAULT
50 = false, WRAP_ONE_PER_LINE, INDENT_ON_COLUMN
52 = false, WRAP_ONE_PER_LINE, INDENT_BY_ONE
81 = true, WRAP_NEXT_PER_LINE, INDENT_DEFAULT
-->
